<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Fossjuvet out-and-back — Vinddalen to first upper-inner Fossjuvet viewpoint [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Vinddalen in Rogaland, take the red T-marked Driftaveien through Fårelia and steep Ytre Fåreliskaret, then continue through Sletteskaret and wet ground to the first upper-inner Fossjuvet viewpoint. Return the same way, about 10.2 km in total. Allow around 4–6 hours plus stops; climbing figures are approximate. Loose stones and wet surfaces need care, and the gorge rim is unfenced. Choose dry, snow-free daylight, stay back from edges and obey closures. The farther bridge, fallhead and Røssdalen circuit are outside this walk.

